%% M1 flow: admin creates a courier (or dispatcher) account.
%% user-service calls the Keycloak Admin REST API through an outbound port (Adapter pattern) using the
%% user-service-admin service account (client credentials). Endpoint: POST /api/v1/admin/users.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Admin (browser)
    participant W as Admin users page<br/>+ BFF
    participant GW as api-gateway
    participant UC as AdminUserController<br/>(api)
    participant S as AdminUserService<br/>(application)
    participant KA as KeycloakAdminAdapter<br/>(IdentityAdminPort)
    participant KC as Keycloak<br/>Admin REST API
    participant DB as users_db
    A->>W: fill form: e-mail, full name, phone, role COURIER, vehicle, home zone, daily capacity
    W->>W: Zod schema validation (same rules as the API)
    W->>GW: POST /api/v1/admin/users (bearer, via BFF)
    GW->>UC: forward (JWT valid)
    UC->>UC: @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')") + Bean Validation: e-mail format, phone ^(\+94|0)7[0-9]{8}$, role in COURIER | DISPATCHER | ADMIN
    alt caller is not ADMIN, or the body is invalid
        UC-->>W: 403 FORBIDDEN or 400 VALIDATION_FAILED problem+json (field names only, values never echoed)
    else valid ADMIN request
        UC->>S: createStaffUser(command)
        S->>KA: createUser(email, name, role)
        opt no cached service-account token
            KA->>KC: POST /realms/swiftdrop/protocol/openid-connect/token grant_type=client_credentials, client user-service-admin
            KC-->>KA: access token (realm-management: manage-users)
        end
        KA->>KC: POST /admin/realms/swiftdrop/users {email, firstName, lastName, enabled}
        alt e-mail already registered
            KC-->>KA: 409 Conflict
            KA-->>S: IdentityConflictException
            S-->>UC: ConflictException EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED
            UC-->>W: 409 problem+json
        else created
            KC-->>KA: 201 Location: .../users/{keycloakId}
            KA->>KC: POST /users/{keycloakId}/role-mappings/realm [COURIER]
            KC-->>KA: 204
            KA->>KC: PUT /users/{keycloakId}/execute-actions-email [UPDATE_PASSWORD]
            KC->>KC: send the set-your-password e-mail through realm SMTP (Mailpit locally), no password ever passes through SwiftDrop
            KC-->>KA: 204
            KA-->>S: keycloakId
            S->>DB: INSERT user_profile (id = keycloakId), user_role, courier_profile (one transaction)
            alt database write fails
                DB-->>S: error
                S->>KA: compensate: deleteUser(keycloakId)
                S-->>UC: ApiException (no half-created account remains)
            else committed
                DB-->>S: ok
                S-->>UC: StaffUser
                UC-->>W: 201 Created, Location /api/v1/admin/users/{id}
                W-->>A: courier listed as 'invitation sent'
            end
        end
    end
